{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1352","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Binary String Reconstruction"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For some binary string $$$s$$$ (i.e. each character $$$s_i$$$ is either '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' or '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"'), all pairs of consecutive (adjacent) characters were written. In other words, all substrings of length $$$2$$$ were written. For each pair (substring of length $$$2$$$), the number of '"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"' (ones) in it was calculated."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given three numbers:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$n_0$$$ — the number of such pairs of consecutive characters (substrings) where the number of ones equals $$$0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$n_1$$$ — the number of such pairs of consecutive characters (substrings) where the number of ones equals $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$n_2$$$ — the number of such pairs of consecutive characters (substrings) where the number of ones equals $$$2$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, for the string $$$s=$$$\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1110011110"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", the following substrings would be written: \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"00"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"01"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"10"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". Thus, $$$n_0=1$$$, $$$n_1=3$$$, $$$n_2=5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to restore "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" suitable binary string $$$s$$$ from the given values $$$n_0, n_1, n_2$$$. It is guaranteed that at least one of the numbers $$$n_0, n_1, n_2$$$ is greater than $$$0$$$. Also, it is guaranteed that a solution exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 1000$$$) — the number of test cases in the input. Then test cases follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case consists of one line which contains three integers $$$n_0, n_1, n_2$$$ ($$$0 \\le n_0, n_1, n_2 \\le 100$$$; $$$n_0 + n_1 + n_2 \\gt 0$$$). It is guaranteed that the answer for given $$$n_0, n_1, n_2$$$ exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print $$$t$$$ lines. Each of the lines should contain a binary string corresponding to a test case. If there are several possible solutions, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n1 3 5\n1 1 1\n3 9 3\n0 1 0\n3 1 2\n0 0 3\n2 0 0\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1110011110\n0011\n0110001100101011\n10\n0000111\n1111\n000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1352F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1352/problem/F"}